{
 "name": "thesis_reads_v2",
 "_comment": [
  "Second thesis read campaign (2026-10-25), after a methodology audit against danluu.com/benchpocalypse",
  "and sled.rs/perf.  Differences from thesis_reads (v1, ran first, unchanged):",
  "  * stock_interior_credit: stock's page cache also gets the dataset's interior-page bytes, which BF keeps",
  "    outside its budget (v100 1.21 MiB, v16 1.43 MiB) -- equal memory for LEAVES.  v1 gave BF 3.8-4.5% more.",
  "  * run with --shuffle (run_thesis_cloud.sh): repeats and SUTs interleaved, so machine drift spreads out",
  "    instead of landing on one SUT.",
  "  * HOLDOUT cells -- shapes no BF setting was tuned on: uniform (negative control: a record cache should",
  "    NOT win), theta 0.7 / 0.99, 200 B values, YCSB B (95/5) and A (50/50) read/update.",
  "  * the other I/O regime: buffered I/O (OS page cache in play, inside the same cgroup cap).",
  "  * one transaction per read (no --read-txn) on the main cell.",
  "Ablations (bf_nofull, bf_noscan, page mode, X1, cap1k) are within-BF comparisons: v1 answers them.",
  "BF runs at the reference's defaults everywhere.  Predictions for C are written before the run (plan)."
 ],
 "datasets": {
  "v100": {
   "records": 4000000,
   "value_len": 100,
   "key_spacing": 16
  },
  "v16": {
   "records": 20000000,
   "value_len": 16,
   "key_spacing": 16
  },
  "v200": {
   "records": 4000000,
   "value_len": 200,
   "key_spacing": 16
  }
 },
 "defaults": {
  "dataset": "v100",
  "repeats": 2,
  "seconds": 60,
  "theta": 0.9,
  "scan_len": 32,
  "synchronous": "normal",
  "journal": "wal",
  "ops_per_txn": 1,
  "read_txn": true,
  "drop_cache": true,
  "budget_bytes": "32M",
  "memmax": "auto",
  "promotion": 30,
  "copy_on_access": 10,
  "direct_io": true,
  "workload": "read=100",
  "stock_interior_credit": true
 },
